# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Bilingual prose for the Tamheed user guide, keyed by the ids docs/guide/render.py asks for.

Rules of this file (tests/test_user_guide.py enforces the first two):
  * every id the page renders has a non-empty "en" and "ar";
  * no key here is unused by the page;
  * identifiers, tool names, column names, statuses and CHECK values are written verbatim inside
    backticks (they render LTR monospace in both languages);
  * a sentence that states an ENGINE mechanism is written after reading the function or trigger it
    names, and the id carries a `# src:` comment naming it;
  * every entry is plain English (check.py lint 14 reads TEXT by import, EN and AR under the
    flavored rules: no semicolon, no sentence over 25 words; plan 188).
Markup allowed in a string: `code`, **bold**, [text](#anchor).

Source notes (2026-10-02). Read directly in tamheed_server.py while authoring: the lesson guard
(L1677-1765: approval needs operator_confirm + confirmed_by, content byte-identical; confirmed_at is
caller-supplied), audit_record (L3241-3287: iteration copied from the header, recorded_at stamped),
_substitute (L701-807: the refusal list), package_close (flushed: false on a moved tree), the
readiness rule closure and the entity_query(type="package") refusal (run live). Column facts
(types, NOT NULL, defaults, CHECK sets, FKs) are derived from the live DDL by extract.py, never typed
here. Other mechanism sentences follow docs/entities.md, references/*.md and the explorer reports.
"""

